 "overview": [
  "Galaxy Sirius is a motor catamaran built in 2024 for Galaxy Cruises, a Galapagos company with a fleet of naturalist and dive boats. She is 36 metres long and 13 metres wide, and Galaxy describes her interior as refined.",
  "She takes 16 guests in nine cabins on the Main and Upper decks, each with a double or twin beds, air conditioning, a safe, a hair dryer, eco-friendly bath products, bathrobes and slippers. There is a bar, a dining room, two lounges, a boutique, a bow solarium and a rooftop jacuzzi.",
  "Two bilingual naturalist guides sail with 16 guests. The 4-night Southern Route runs from San Cristobal to Baltra via Espanola, Floreana, Santa Fe and South Plaza. The 5-night Western Route covers Isabela and Fernandina. The 5-night Northern Route ends at San Cristobal after Genovesa. The three link into longer trips."
 ],
 "why": [
  "Galaxy also includes the VIP lounge at Baltra and San Cristobal airports.",
  "The routes chain by day of the week: Southern into Western into Northern makes 14 nights, and the Northern Route reaches Genovesa."
 ],
